  "full_text": "So, entertain God and your ass will follow. God wants praise. I thought that zoos and telescopes were really good because they cause praise of God. Then I thought, oh, maybe he doesn't. He wasn't, maybe he's shy. He wasn't really on board. He wasn't like, oh yeah, do that, do that, do that. But, you know, I asked him, His favorite toy for a kid, and he said a magnifying glass. So I think God likes, oh, if we want to make God happy, oh, let's go check this shit out. Let's go find something that makes Mr. God happy. He wants praise. You know, I never did this before. I never did this before. Wow. Look at the color. Can you see the color? Wow. So, I think there's a problem with dignity. This is bad. This is bad. Dignity. God says. God says. You're in good hands. Bless the Lord, all you his host, who serve him in doing his will. What does it mean to say if God is faithful? It means he is steadfast in his allegiance to his people. He will not leave us in a lurch. It also means he is firm in his adherence to his promises. He keeps his word. Faithfulness suggests the idea of loyalty, dependability, constancy, being resolute, steady, and consistent. God isn't fickle. No hot and cold temperature moods with him. God is also faithful to remember his servants. He remembers our works, each individual act. He takes note of the love within us that prompted the deed. No one on earth can do these special things. We forget, but God remembers. We see the action. God sees the motive. This qualifies him as the best record keeper and judge. He alone is perfect and consistently just. You're in good hands with the Almighty.",
